\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Hierarchical coefficients close; these do not}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{On the hierarchical precision of \ref{fdip-009A}, the block
means return a precision of the same shape, with coefficients
#{c'_i=pc_{i+1}}. The limit precision in \ref{fdip-00BT} does
not. For #{B=4} and for #{B=5} the only undirected distance
beyond #{1} is distance #{2}, so that entry is the nonzero
one. For #{B\ge 6} the same argument shows that some distance
at least #{2} carries a nonzero coefficient, and it does not
by itself name the distance.}
